    "explanation": "Each example row shows one jigsaw piece changing a board. The dark piece rotates the board a quarter-turn anticlockwise. The dotted piece colours black only the shape in the middle-right square: the same shape elsewhere stays white. The striped piece copies the shape in the middle-right square into the empty centre square. In the question the pieces snap together as the dotted piece, then the dark piece, then the striped piece. Follow them in that order, using the board each piece leaves for the next piece. The board after the last piece is the missing one.",
